    <!-- Systemic Gap Section -->
    <section class="gap-section">
        <div class="container">
            <h2>Why is there such a systemic technology gap in the social sector?</h2>
            <p>When the world's biggest servers hum to open-source code, it's ironic non-profits still run on Google Sheets.</p>
            <p>Experiments had already started in 2021 by FOSS United, Tech4Good community, FOSS united, Reap Benefit, Aikyam Fellows and TinkerHub in the form of tech volunteering, some software development, partnering with various NGOs.</p>
            <p>What began as scattered experiments and caffeine-fueled conversations, slowly drew a circle of like-minded tinkers, people trying in their own corners, to gather at the Zerodha office, J.P. Nagar one fine day. They decided to build meaningful tech muscle for the social sector.</p>
            <p>While unpacking social sector roadblocks one filter coffee at a time, we realised the fixes couldn't come from quick hacks. Addressing these challenges requires a multi-faceted approach, one that turns digital potential from a 'good-to-have' into an absolute essential.</p>
            <p>Soon after, the group was formalized as an alliance, OASIS (Open-source Alliance for Social Innovation and Sustainability).</p>
        </div>
